+
+## Built State (F027, 2026-09-26)
+
+What exists on disk at the close of F027, built in nine rounds over two sessions on
+`feature/f027-task-veto`, cut from `main` at `557cbbcc`. Every DECISION named lives in
+`.agent/decisions.md`; every round's verdict in `.agent/live_review.md` or, once rotated, its
+archive.
+
+**T001 — the command, the reason and the state change.** `packages/orchestration/task_veto.py`
+records a veto as a create-only control file per task under the job's `vetoed_tasks/`, never in
+the job record, with the reason kept verbatim: `validate_veto_reason` refuses a blank reason, one
+over 500 characters, and one holding a control character or secret-shaped text, rather than store
+it altered. The pure gate `veto_refusal` admits a pending, running, blocked, failed or skipped task
+of an unfinished job and refuses every other case with a named code; `veto_unreachable` is
+`dag_schedule.blocked_downstream` over the vetoed tasks; every accepted veto writes one
+`task_vetoed` event carrying the reason, the actor and the unreachable set; and there is no
+un-veto (DECISION F027 D1). The linear runner folds a veto before its task loop and at every
+pre-task safe point: an active attempt first has its workspace returned to its start tree by
+`worktrees.restore_tree`, the task becomes `vetoed`, its unreachable set is never dispatched,
+independent tasks run on, and a run whose remaining work is all vetoed or unreachable ends
+`blocked` with `all_remaining_work_vetoed` naming both sets (DECISION F027 D2). A task vetoed while
+its provider call runs finishes that call and is halted at the next in-task safe point; the cycle
+executor withholds a vetoed task and its dependents at every pick (DECISION F027 D3).
+
+**T002 — the unreachable set, the evidence and the proposal.** Every veto files one decision of
+type `replan_proposal` with the id `veto:<request id>`, built by
+`packages/orchestration/veto_proposal.py` from the control files and never stored in the job
+record; its summary reads "You vetoed <task> — reason: <reason>", and it offers
+`replan_follow_up` or `accept_reduced_scope` with plain-words labels. An answer is a create-only
+control fact under `veto_answers/`: a replan creates a follow-up job, unplanned, whose prompt
+carries the vetoed work, the reason and the unreachable work, and nothing runs it; once every veto
+is answered, the linear runner's next run completes the job with the reduced scope (DECISION F027
+D4). The task-expectation tables of `packages/orchestration/run_manifest.py` read `vetoed` beside
+the statuses a task with no finalized call may carry.
+
+**T003 — the channel, the page and the end-to-end.** `job.veto-task` is a catalog command, the CLI
+verb `remedy job veto-task <job> <task> --reason <text>` in `apps/cli/commands/job_veto_cmd.py`,
+and a clause of the write door that checks the reason's shape before the job is read; the door's
+`decision.resolve` answers a `veto:` decision, which makes the inbox card answerable (DECISIONs F027
+D5 and D6). The dashboard's `vetoes` section carries each veto's reason, actor, time, request id and
+unreachable set, the vetoable tasks and the answer; the page seeds and streams a vetoed task's node
+as `vetoed`, with the strike the glyph language already held; the job's text report prints
+`Vetoed by <actor>: <reason>` under the task and its export carries a `veto` object; both veto
+event names are in the page's catalog (DECISION F027 D7). The live canvas fades the unreachable set
+by the vetoed treatment's own `downstreamAlpha`, hover text names the reason or the vetoing task as
+plain text, the detail popover shows a Veto or an Unreachable section with buttons that open the
+task on the other side, and a "Veto task" form sends the veto through
+`apps/ui/src/api/vetoSend.ts` (DECISION F027 D8). `tests/ui_server/test_task_veto_e2e_live.py`
+drives an approved diamond through `python3 -m apps.cli.main job run` and a live door: a veto of
+one branch on a job paused after its first task, the other branch completing, the job blocked with
+the veto named, the proposal open, and both answers carried to their effects (DECISION F027 D9).
+
+**Acceptance, by the test that proves it.** The empty reason refused at the schema:
+`TestVetoReason` in `tests/orchestration/test_task_veto.py`, the door's 400 on the `reason` field
+in `tests/ui_server/test_command_dispatch.py` and the CLI's `TestVetoRefusalExitCodes` in
+`tests/cli/test_job_veto.py`. The diamond
+exact — strike, unreachable set, sibling completion, terminal accounting: `TestDiamondVetoBeforeTheRun`
+and `TestInFlightVetoOfTheRunningTask` in `tests/orchestration/test_task_veto_runner.py`, the
+cycle executor's in `tests/orchestration/test_task_veto_cycles.py`, the seeded and streamed node in
+`brainView.test.ts` and `brainReducer.test.ts`, and the end-to-end. Nothing replans without the
+answer, and both options' effects: `TestAccept`, `TestReplan` and `TestRepeatedAnswer` in
+`tests/orchestration/test_veto_proposal.py`, `TestSettledCompletion` and the end-to-end's two tests.
+The reason verbatim in audit, report and hover: `TestTaskVetoedEvent`, `TestReportCarriesTheVeto`,
+`tests/ui_server/test_dashboard_vetoes.py` and `vetoView.test.ts`, and the end-to-end reads a reason
+holding `<`, `&` and double quotes byte for byte from the door to the report. Each round's mutation
+proofs are its `.agent/authored/f027-r<n>-mutations.py`.
+
+**Modules and lists (closure precondition 7).** F027 added `packages/orchestration/task_veto.py`,
+`packages/orchestration/veto_proposal.py` and `apps/cli/commands/job_veto_cmd.py`, and their three
+lines in `tests/orchestration/import_reachability_allowlist.txt`; nothing joined `ALLOWED_UNWIRED`
+or `RESERVED_NAMESPACES` in `tests/test_no_orphan_modules.py`. Its other new modules are TypeScript
+under `apps/ui/src/`: `api/vetoView.ts`, `api/vetoSend.ts` and `components/detail/TaskVetoForm.tsx`.
+
+**Beyond the code.** `docs/guides/exit-codes.md` lists `remedy job veto-task`. Two rows of
+`docs/ui/design_reference/assumption_log.md` record the canvas hover text and the popover's Veto and
+Unreachable sections with the form, none of which the design reference drew. The write door's
+import guard in `tests/ui_server/test_command_channel.py` skips the body of an `if TYPE_CHECKING:`
+block, because a type-only import never runs (DECISION F027 D6).
+
+**Deliberate absences.** No un-veto: the replan is the recovery. No mid-run replanning: the
+follow-up job is created unplanned and only a person plans and runs it. The cycle executor withholds
+vetoed work but never settles a job whose vetoes are answered; that completion belongs to the linear
+runner. The simple graph view shows no veto, because it draws no state glyph at all.
+
+**Findings.** F027 registered R-1065 to R-1070, and all six are resolved: R-1065 a retried veto's
+refusal shape, R-1066 a directory where a restored file stood, R-1067 the CLI naming the wrong
+relaunch command, R-1068 the page's event catalog missing both veto events, R-1069 two shipped
+sentences naming a rule and a module that do not exist, and R-1070 a lead-in with no list under it.
+No finding was open at F027's claim.
